envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-model
type: schema
id: model
context: >-
  guardian/schemas — sovereign local copy. Origin: lib/node-schemas/schema.model (shared
  canonical version, may have moved on independently since this copy was made — sovereignty means
  guardian does not depend on it at runtime, not that the two can never drift).
intent: null
summary: null
system: guardian
tags: []
exported_at: 1789239046422
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    ollama/config.js — the one real place model tags live (DEFAULT_MODEL/FALLBACK_MODEL).
    Guardian's own use: guardian.node-taxonomy.md marks this READS — guardian never authors a
    standalone .model record itself, it only ever sees a model tag as a field inside a hat
    (guardian/lib/jobs.js calls hatForge.get(name), and a hat's own model field is an Ollama tag).
    Materialized as a local copy for the same reason schema.hat already has one despite guardian
    also being READS-only for hats: guardian resolves every type it touches, read or write,
    without a runtime dependency on lib/node-schemas.js. Leaving model out while hat was already
    in would have been an inconsistent, unexplained gap in guardian's own sovereign set.
  fields:
    tag:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: a real, verified Ollama model tag, e.g. "mistral:7b-instruct-q4_K_M"
    role:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: "'default' | 'fallback' — which real config slot this fills"
    envVar:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: the real env var that overrides this tag, if any
